---
import ServiceLayout from '../../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
import MediaSection from '../../components/MediaSection.astro';
import PhotoPair from '../../components/PhotoPair.astro';
import MidCTA from '../../components/MidCTA.astro';
import { industries } from '../../data/industries';
import hero from '../../assets/industries/corporate-offices/office-lounge-vending.png';
import officeLounge from '../../assets/industries/corporate-offices/office-lounge.png';
import smartFridge from '../../assets/industries/corporate-offices/office-smart-fridge.webp';
import meetingSalads from '../../assets/industries/corporate-offices/office-meeting-salads.jpg';
import teamBreak from '../../assets/industries/corporate-offices/team-break.jpg';
import officeLunch from '../../assets/industries/corporate-offices/office-lunch.jpg';

const faqs = [
	{
		question: 'Does our office qualify for free vending?',
		answer:
			'An office qualifies with at least 50 people in total foot traffic, counting employees and visitors. Equipment, delivery, and setup then cost $0, with no installation fee, no service fee, and no long-term contract.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Is office coffee service free?',
		answer:
			'Coffee machine installation is free. Coffee, tea, and supplies are paid. Brands include Starbucks, Ellis Coffee, and Rooted Grounds Coffee Co.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Can we offer snacks and meals as an employee perk?',
		answer:
			'Yes. Subsidized vending is available on request. The company covers part of the price, so employees pay less at the machine or market.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Can employees request specific products?',
		answer:
			'Yes. We track what sells and listen to requests. Specific products and brands are added when there is enough demand.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Do you serve offices on several floors or in shared buildings?',
		answer:
			'Yes. We walk the building first and recommend where equipment should go. Service visits are planned around your hours and building access rules.',
	},
];
---

<ServiceLayout
	title="Corporate Office Vending Services in DFW"
	description="Free smart coolers, micro markets, vending, and coffee machine setup for Dallas–Fort Worth corporate offices. Cashless, fresh food, and no long-term contract."
	h1="Corporate Office Vending Services in DFW"
	eyebrow="Corporate Offices"
	intro="Texas Vending stocks Dallas–Fort Worth offices with smart coolers, micro markets, vending machines, and coffee, so teams can grab breakfast, lunch, or a snack without leaving the building. Placement is free at qualifying offices, and there is no long-term contract."
	heroImage={hero}
	heroAlt="Office lounge with people on sofas and two smart vending coolers behind them"
	serviceType="Corporate office vending services"
	crumb="Corporate Offices"
	parent={{ name: 'Industries We Serve', url: '/industries-we-serve/' }}
	related={{ heading: 'Other Industries We Serve', items: industries }}
	faqs={faqs}
	cta={{
		heading: 'Upgrade Your Office Break Room',
		text: 'Tell us your headcount, floors, and office hours. We will walk the space and recommend the right setup. No cost for equipment and no long-term contract.',
	}}
>
	<MediaSection image={officeLounge} alt="Coworkers brainstorming in a bright office lounge with bean bags and a coffee bar" heading="Keeping Teams in the Office Through the Day" eyebrow="The challenge">
		<p>
			Offices ask more of the break room than they used to. Teams come in for meetings, client visits, and collaboration
			days, and they expect the office to make that easy. A lunch run that eats an hour, or a coffee line down the
			street, pulls people out of the building at the times you most want them together.
		</p>
		<p>
			Office managers and HR teams also have enough to manage. Ordering snacks, restocking a fridge, and chasing
			reimbursements is time taken from real work. A break room that stocks itself solves both problems.
		</p>
		<p>
			Visitors notice the break room too. A client waiting for a meeting or a candidate on interview day sees an empty,
			cash-only machine very differently from a clean cooler of fresh food and a working coffee machine.
		</p>
	</MediaSection>

	<MediaSection image={smartFridge} alt="Coworkers sharing lunch at a table near a touch-screen smart fridge" heading="Break Room Options for Every Office Size" eyebrow="What we install" reverse>
		<p>The right setup depends on your space, headcount, and how your office uses its break room:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><a href="/our-services/ai-smart-cooler/">AI smart coolers</a> for fresh meals in a small kitchen or pantry</li>
			<li><a href="/our-services/micro-markets/">Micro markets</a> for larger cafés with open shelves and self-checkout</li>
			<li><a href="/our-services/vending-machine/">Snack and drink vending machines</a> for lobbies and side break areas</li>
			<li><a href="/our-services/coffee-water/">Coffee machines and water</a> with Starbucks, Ellis Coffee, and Rooted Grounds Coffee Co.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Smart coolers unlock with a tap and charge automatically for what is taken. Put an item back before the door
			closes, and you are not charged. Our <a href="/fresh-food/">fresh food menu</a> covers sandwiches, wraps, salads,
			yogurt, fruit cups, and better-for-you drinks for working lunches.
		</p>
		<h3>Fitting a Multi-Floor Office</h3>
		<p>
			In a building with several floors, one break room may be an elevator ride away for half the staff. We look at where
			teams sit and meet, then tell you whether a smart cooler on a second floor or a coffee station near the conference
			rooms would get more use than one larger setup. Shared buildings often have rules for deliveries and loading
			docks, and we plan around them.
		</p>
	</MediaSection>

	<PhotoPair
		photos={[
			{
				image: meetingSalads,
				alt: 'Coworkers in a meeting with packaged salads and bottled water on the table',
				caption: 'Salads and bottled water make a working lunch easy to pull together.',
			},
			{
				image: teamBreak,
				alt: 'Coworkers talking around a table of snacks and drinks in an office',
				caption: 'A stocked break room gives teams a reason to gather and talk.',
			},
		]}
	/>
	<MidCTA />


	<MediaSection image={officeLunch} alt="Coworkers chatting over coffee and pastries in a bright office café" heading="Service That Stays Out of Your Way" eyebrow="How we serve offices">
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Stocked on real data.</strong> Equipment reports sales in real time, so we restock what is running low and drop what does not sell.</li>
			<li><strong>Visits that fit your building.</strong> We set a restocking schedule for your office and plan around your hours, security desk, and badge rules.</li>
			<li><strong>Cashless.</strong> Cards, mobile wallets, and tap-to-pay on every machine, micro market, and coffee system.</li>
			<li><strong>Subsidized vending on request.</strong> Lower prices for your team as a workplace perk.</li>
			<li><strong>24-hour response.</strong> Local technicians respond to reported issues within 24 hours, including after hours.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Office attendance can swing from day to day with hybrid schedules. Real-time sales data lets us stock for your busy
			days instead of guessing, so Tuesday lunch does not sell out and Friday food does not go to waste.
		</p>
		<p>
			Coffee often matters most. We install the machine at no cost, and you pay for the coffee, tea, and supplies you
			use. Pick from Starbucks, Ellis Coffee, or Rooted Grounds Coffee Co. based on what your team likes.
		</p>
		<p>
			Switching from another provider? Our <a href="/blog/vending-contract-checklist/">vending contract checklist</a> shows what to look for before you sign.
		</p>
	</MediaSection>
</ServiceLayout>
